From: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sound: oss3: T33 (PRJ008) audio driver at the vendor module's release

The T33 vendor stack loads audio.ko (jzsound oss3, AUDIO_DRIVER_VERSION
H20250929a) built from the PRJ008 host (AIC) + inner codec sources. This tree
carries the same version string but an older/other variant of those files
(codec "fast init" path without the codec power-up delays, no mpll parent for
the spk/mic clocks on 3.10, no Ref-Loop FIFO pop after the playback stop).

Bring audio_dsp.c, include/audio_{dsp,common}.h, host/PRJ008/audio_aic.c and
inner_codecs/PRJ008/codec.c to the GPL oss3 sources of the Ingenic T33 SDK
2.0.0 (Tassadar 20260804, opensource/drivers/audio/oss3). A PRJ008 build of
them is string- and symbol-identical to the vendor audio.ko of the JZT33L
module (only compiler-generated .isra/.constprop suffixes differ).
Only PRJ008 is built on T33 (sound/oss3/Makefile).

Signed-off-by: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
